// The disk's thickness: a thin sheet of particles overall, but noticeably
// thicker near the core (y_thickness falls linearly from 300 milli-units at
// r=0 to 60 at max_radius()), with the actual vertical offset a PRNG sample
// in -thickness..+thickness (noise_range, galaxy/math/rng/lset.id).

particle_y(int r) {
  int thick = y_thickness(r);
} return int noise_range(thick);

y_thickness(int r) {
  int t = 300 - r * 240 / max_radius();
} return int t;
